<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.15;" data-page-h1>
          Tee-time booking and payments platform for golf courses
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-0" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 980px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);">
          A serverless first booking platform built for &ldquo;tee time drops&rdquo; with strict tenant isolation, distributed locking, and POS/payment integrations that survive peak traffic.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The problem</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            Public and private golf courses face extreme traffic bursts (e.g., 7:00 AM &ldquo;tee time drops&rdquo;). Legacy monolithic platforms suffered race conditions, resulting in double bookings
            and lost revenue.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            The platform required a multi tenant architecture that could scale to hundreds of courses while maintaining strict data isolation for each course&rsquo;s financial records.
            Under peak traffic, the system must guarantee atomic bookings without degrading UX through heavy database locks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <%= render "home/case_studies/at_a_glance",
            industry: "Golf / hospitality SaaS",
            client: "GolfPay360",
            country: "[[AHMAD: country]]",
            what_we_built: "Multi-tenant tee-time booking with distributed locking and POS payments",
            integrations: "Clover/Square POS SDKs, Stripe Terminal (card present), Twilio Programmable Messaging",
            stack: "Next.js, AWS Lambda, DynamoDB" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="what-we-built">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we built</h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          We architected a serverless first booking platform designed for high concurrency event handling. By moving away from a traditional database locking model and toward event sourced
          patterns, we eliminated collision errors during peak traffic.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          The system separates browse from commit: availability is edge optimized for low latency reads, while booking writes are protected by distributed locks and idempotent retries.
          This keeps the tee sheet fast worldwide while guaranteeing atomic bookings at the point of transaction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How it works</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-4" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Distributed locking:</strong> Redis based Redlock ensures atomic booking operations across multiple server instances.</li>
          <li><strong>Edge optimized availability:</strong> CloudFront Functions serve tee sheet availability from the nearest edge location, reducing latency globally.</li>
          <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> Next.js (Frontend) &rarr; AWS Lambda &rarr; DynamoDB (NoSQL for sub millisecond lookups).</li>
          <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Clover/Square POS SDKs; Stripe Terminal for card present transactions; Twilio Programmable Messaging.</li>
          <li><strong>Security:</strong> Designed to support PCI DSS; strict per tenant isolation; JWT based RBAC.</li>
          <li><strong>AI features:</strong> Dynamic yield management suggests real time price surges/discounts using weather data and historical no show rates.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Results</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-0" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Higher digital adoption:</strong> shifted the majority of bookings from phone to web/app.</li>
          <li><strong>Prevents double bookings:</strong> distributed locking + idempotent retries protect commit paths under load.</li>
          <li><strong>Reduced administrative overhead:</strong> automated check ins and self service rescheduling cut manual work.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/gallery", slug: "golfpay360-saas" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/client_quote", slug: "golfpay360-saas" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/cta", blurb: "We&rsquo;ll design concurrency, inventory locking, and payment flows to survive real peak traffic." %>

  <section class="py-4 bg-white">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <%= link_to "B2B SaaS →", industry_b2b_saas_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>